WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.730
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.320
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.280
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.950
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.370
Kana

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.710
Chiaki

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.500
Haruka

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Boss of Ball-Kicking Once Again

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.810
Hey, it turned out better than I expected!

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.100
Hey Keiko, how did you do on your test?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.020
What about you?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.980
65 percent!

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.650
I was expecting to fail, so I guess I did all right.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.570
R-Right.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.200
So, what about you?

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.450
H-Hundred percent...

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:27.870
Huh?

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.670
A hundred out of a hundred?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.840
That would mean a bull's-eye each time?

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.300
No misses at all?

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.090
A perfect score?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.430
Umm...

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.060
That's incredibly boring!

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.930
What an uninteresting score!

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.690
If you're so good with numbers, you should just become a calculator, you damn calculator!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.310
You don't need to be so harsh...

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.070
But this 65 percent, in comparison...

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.530
My score seems more human.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.570
Picking a fight with a calculator is no fun.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.370
I should find someone whom I stand a chance against...

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.200
Hey, Minami.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.700
How did your test go?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.410
So you came, Big Boss!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.620
Do you feel like challenging me again?

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.710
Eh? Boss?

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.550
So, how many marks did you get?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.670
Tell me.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.670
C'mon, I'll beat you easily.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.090
Spit it out, now!

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.720
Uh, no, I didn't mean it as a challenge...

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.510
I got 66 percent...

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.940
Fujioka-kun, you didn't have to be so harsh...

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.020
Eh?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.940
Did I say something wrong?

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.780
No... Not yet...

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.110
I haven't lost just yet!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.570
Current Record:

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.780
1 Win 1 Loss

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.320
The current score is still one-all.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.990
Don't think that you've won!

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.330
Eh? When did I lose?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.750
Let's decide the winner with the English test scores!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.670
Well, I'm fine with that...

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.040
Then, let's decide the penalty for losing.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.090
How about the loser pretends to be a dog?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.920
Hey, Kana!

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.090
Alright. Let's go with that...

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.430
Don't chicken out, okay?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.260
You'll be stretching out your paw to me later.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.730
Well, that seems about right.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.480
What about you, Keiko?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.860
Eh? Uh... Umm...

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:21.990
Hundred percent...

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.860
You should just go to America.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.160
61 percent...

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.160
Although it's a mark overflowing with humanity...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.630
I got a 65 just before, anyway...

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.300
Oh yeah, just then that guy got 66 marks, didn't he?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.940
Minami!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.100
How did you do?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.600
I see you came, Fujioka.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.610
First, tell me what you got.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.860
I got 69 percent.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.530
I lost...

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.280
And you even altered it twice...

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.570
Eh? I won?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.580
Then...

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.950
Not yet!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.620
The real battle begins now!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.650
I... I lost...

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.270
Even after you altered the score so many times...

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.190
I won, didn't I?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.400
But it's a promise, right?

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.820
Your paw.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.160
Minami...

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.250
That's your foot...

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.000
Since these are called the front paws,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.130
The hands are also feet!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.380
And the feet are also feet!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.550
Huh?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.340
Minami-ke!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.850
Oh yeah, Chiaki,

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.720
Can I ask you something?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:57.980
What?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.520
How have you been scoring on your tests lately?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.240
These prawn-mayonnaise-flavored crackers are really tasty.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.370
You're right! It's good!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.340
Why did you change the subject?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.300
Because I don't think anything good will come of it.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:36.640
That might not be the case.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.860
You're horrible!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.530
Were you thinking that not getting a hundred marks would make you more human?!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.500
Finishing my milk without asking and calling me horrible on top of that...

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.590
I knew nothing good would come out of this.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.100
With this, we're even.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.180
What are you saying?

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.440
I haven't lost yet, okay?

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.480
Did you get poor marks for your tests?

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.270
They're not poor at all!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.360
Those are splendid marks filled with human warmth!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.120
Don't let it get to your head with just 97 percent!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.240
Keiko got a hundred percent, okay?!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.040
How many marks did you get?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.120
I'll kill you!

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.110
What do you think?

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.780
Do you understand how scary I am now?

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:11.820
Are you fine with that?

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.070
Haruka-neesama said that she's going to make cream stew tonight.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.700
Nee-sama couldn't have imagined that a carton that was full in the morning,

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.460
would become empty by evening.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.170
I just need to go buy one, right?!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.970
What's wrong?

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.350
My stomach's churning... I feel sick.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.060
The milk's a stupid!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.190
You're the stupid one.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.730
Ah, what's that?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.150
Chiaki is always studying quietly.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.280
Don't say "quietly".

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.320
Sneakily?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.700
Are your scores really that poor?

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.700
I told you they're not poor!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.830
Those are passionate marks filled with my heart!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.500
You try to get good marks by studying for the tests just coming up.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.380
That spirit is wrong to begin with.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.180
Are these ordinary opinions all that you can give?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.970
What did you just say?

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.060
The man who'll take you as his bride is an unfortunate person.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.770
What are you talking about?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.770
A newlywed life born from those ordinary opinions can't possibly be interesting.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.150
Don't go fantasizing and deciding on my future on your own.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.780
That goes for cooking too!

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:42.530
You can't cook anything that could touch the hearts of people!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.450
I don't really care if I can move other people or not.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.210
So, your husband won't know how it feels to be moved,

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.330
And will live an unfortunate life.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.710
You can make something, can't you?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:11:01.140
You, who aren't ordinary, can cook something which can touch the hearts of people, right?

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.140
Of... Of course.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:09.310
Then, show me!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.190
S-Sure, I'll make you something.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:18.490
Whenever a new recipe is invented, it's not the result of common sense, but of a sudden spark of ideas!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.490
<i>You idiot.</i>

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:24.070
<i>That sudden spark of ideas you had was what gave birth to that disgusting stew back then.</i>

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.410
<i>Have you forgotten already?</i>

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.880
I'm back!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.380
Oh my... I'm sorry, you got tired of waiting?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.300
What did you make?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.720
Gratin? Tempura? Are the leftovers for me?

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.680
I'll help with the cream stew.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.430
I'm going to buy some milk.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.320
Thank you for the food!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.950
The winner: Haruka-neesama.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.740
<i>I... I lost...</i>

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.580
<i>A mere cream stew is able to melt the hearts of people to this extent?</i>

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.290
Eh? When did I fall asleep?

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.210
You're awake?

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.790
Damn you, Fujioka!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.710
Attacking when your enemy is sleeping is a cowardly act!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.670
Fight me fair and square!

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.680
You got it wrong!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.390
The next lesson is now music...

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.770
And you were still here napping.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:15.350
I wanted to wake you up, but you looked like you were enjoying your nap...

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.280
Y-You really are suspicious...

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.820
Well, forget it.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.030
Ah!

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.030
Minami!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:29.950
What?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.410
I didn't have a chance to tell you something, so I'll be frank now...

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.080
I...

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:42.300
...really like you.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.720
...like you...

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.560
Chiaki-sama!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.270
Is Chiaki-sama home?!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.070
What's wrong? You're making so much noise.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.980
Ah, there you are!

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.860
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:10.910
Today in school, the Ball-Kicking Boss told me that he's fallen in love with me.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.660
There was the love letter last time too...

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.460
What exactly is going on?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.130
That means he likes you, doesn't it?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.300
Don't talk crap!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:27.800
I'm sorry! I got carried away.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.760
So, under what kind of situation did he say that?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.310
Damn you, Fujioka!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:42.820
I was taking a nap in the classroom, and he was about to attack me in my sleep.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:46.070
Then I told him to fight me fair and square, I guess.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.690
I get it.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:52.740
Which means to say, you were attacked in your sleep, and you were taken aback by that.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:55.990
Hence you were swayed by his words.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.420
To the point where even your senses were paralyzed...

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.290
Wha... What... Does that mean?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:06.460
The moment after you heard his words of love for you, your mind stopped working.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.640
You should try to recall what the Boss said after that.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.720
Come to think of it, he could have said something else...

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:21.230
Judging from the situation, most likely he said this:

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.730
You've let you defenses fall.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.450
I see!

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.990
That's so embarrassing!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.870
I can't believe I've mistaken him twice!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.330
Was I thirsty for it?

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.620
Was I yearning for it?

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:44.330
Something sweet and sour like a confession?!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:47.750
But now you understand what you have to do, right?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.100
Say, do you have soccer club training today?

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.680
Yeah.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.480
Good morning, Kana.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.860
Good morning.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.270
The first lesson is Mathematics.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.900
Have you done your homework?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.400
Ah, what homework?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.650
Minami...

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:12.570
Good morning!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.390
<i>She hates me now.</i>

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.350
Minami-ke!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.360
I'm back.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:57.120
Ah, hello. Sorry to intrude.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.950
Hello.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.870
Hey!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:05.540
I bought drinks!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.460
Hey, Kana, who's he?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.920
Ah, Chiaki, welcome back.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.220
That's Fujioka.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.590
Fujioka?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.090
That boss of the...?

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:20.180
Why is the Boss in our house?

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.680
Regarding that...

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.440
It's not like I want to pick a fight with him and become the new boss.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.690
Rather, I'd like to avoid unnecessary conflicts if possible too.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:33.070
Back to the point, didn't we make too much curry yesterday?

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.250
Eh? It's somewhat watery.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.120
Add more curry powder.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:53.840
Eh? This time it became too thick.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.550
No choice but to dilute it.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.680
Eh? It's somewhat watery.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.680
Add more curry powder.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.850
It became too thick again.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.770
No choice but to dilute it.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.190
It's watery.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.650
Add more curry powder.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:13.820
It's watery!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.360
Dilute it.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:24.450
Why did you end up making three pots of curry?

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:31.540
It's a plan to make use of the curry I made too much of to get on better terms with the Boss.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.550
This is truly killing two birds with one stone!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.970
And the Boss came along with you so readily?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:44.470
<i>I thought Minami didn't like me anymore, but that doesn't seem to be the case.</i>

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:45.850
<i>Thank God!</i>

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.850
<i>No, that's not all.</i>

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.650
<i>To get invited for dinner is really something!</i>

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:54.650
<i>I can get closer to her in one shot!</i>

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.480
Here, have some green tea.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.450
<i>He must be up to something...</i>

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.080
<i>This person...</i>

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.290
I'm back!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.080
Eh? Really?

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.420
No, it's a joke! How could that be for real?

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:20.010
So you see, Haruka-neesama's curry is really delicious.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.600
What? If you have any complaints, don't eat that.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:25.560
Are you okay with that?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.730
There are still two more pots. You want them all to yourself?

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.060
I'm sorry! I said something conceited.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:38.820
Fujioka is really a nice person, isn't he?

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:43.280
Yeah. I can't believe he's a gang leader, it must've been a misunderstanding.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.870
Also... How should I put it...

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.950
He feels just like Dad.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.130
Was Dad something like that?

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.840
Ninomiya-kun!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:02.970
Sensei.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.680
Sensei!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.270
Ninomiya-kun!

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.350
Sensei!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:15.560
Ninomiya-kun!!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.190
Sensei and Ninomiya-kun. Please look forward to the continuation.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.200
It's already this late? It's about time I...

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.870
What's the matter? That's not like you.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:34.500
Say whatever you want to say.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.920
That's my seat.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.550
Ah, I'm sorry. I'm leaving now.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.600
Oh my! I'm so sorry about that.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.020
Is that so?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:01.690
By the way, are you in any clubs?

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.610
Yes. I'm in the soccer club.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.280
Wow, the soccer club!

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.530
What's your position?

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.620
Are you a regular?

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.410
Yes, more or less.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.370
I'm okay anywhere in the front of the field.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.290
That's wonderful!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.750
<i>What's with this heartwarming atmosphere?</i>

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.010
<i>could this by any chance be...</i>

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:29.140
<i>A plan to make not only me an ally, but also Haruka and Chiaki...</i>

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:32.390
<i>A plan to kill three birds with one stone?!</i>

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:37.600
Get out!!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.360
Here, something for you to take home.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:44.690
Get out! Get out! Get out! Get out! Get out!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.450
Get out! Get out!

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.160
Come visit again, okay?

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.120
Huh?!

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:33.890
Love takes as many forms as there are people.

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.430
Next time, The Pattern of Love.

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.180
It's a beautiful tale of love.

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.770
You're serious even in the episode preview, Keiko. You're really lacking a human touch.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:43.190
You can just go join a government-controlled TV station.
